body:
Hello I'm trying to implement a search filtered by date that works with pagination and it's impossible to make them work together. Note: I am using instantSearch router to save queries in URL and trigger them onLoad.

```js
// 1. Pagination is working (using refine(n) in a custom pagination widget) but date filters are not set yet
helper.search();

// 2. Filters are working but pagination is not working (no Call made to Algolia when using pagination)
helper.setQueryParameter('filters', 'date_timestamp:1538352000 TO 1540944000')
  .search();


/* The next solutions to make date filters + pagination are not working */

// Same result as 2.
helper.setQueryParameter('filters', 'date_timestamp:1538352000 TO 1540944000')
  .setPage(helper.state.page)
  .search();

// Same result as 1.
helper.search(helper.state.query, {
  page: helper.state.page,
  filters: 'date_timestamp:1538352000 TO 1540944000',
})

// Seems to be working but 'helper.state.page' is not incremented when calling refine(n) in my custom widget
helper.setQueryParameter("filters", filters)
  .setQueryParameter("page", helper.state.page)
  .search()
```

How am I supposed to make filtering and pagination work in the same search ?
I am using **algoliasearch@4.8.0**.
